James sought clarity in describing data from the EM-DAT database regarding flooding in Bangladesh. Initial wording suggested confusion over the number affected, as he wanted to ensure it reflected over 5 million people affected in each of five different years, rather than a total. After clarifications about the total number of flooding events, they arrived at a well-structured sentence: "These risks are already manifesting, with six flooding events that each affected over 5 million people in Bangladesh over the last decade (Delforge 2025)." Arachne provided feedback and options to enhance readability and accuracy throughout the discussion.
